  "paper_id": "asplos-2023-heron-automatically-constrained-high-performance-library-5c73b1a3",
  "title": "Heron: Automatically Constrained High-performance Library Generation for Deep Learning Accelerators",
  "abstract": "Deep Learning Accelerators (DLAs) are effective to improve both performance and energy efficiency of compute-intensive deep learning algorithms. A flexible and portable mean to exploit DLAs is using high-performance software libraries with well-established APIs, which are typically either manually implemented or automatically generated by exploration-based compilation approaches. Though exploration-based approaches significantly reduce programming efforts, they fail to find optimal or near-optimal programs from a large but low-quality search space because the massive inherent constraints of DLAs cannot be accurately characterized.",
  "abstract_source_id": "src-abstract-asplos-2023-5c73b1a3",
